          "source_quote": "ἐγὼ δὲ ἀγνοῶν ὅλον τὸ πρᾶγμα ὡς μαινομένην ἀπεσειόμην",
          "english_quote": "Knowing nothing of the whole situation, I shook her off as though she were mad;",
          "issue": "“I shook her off” presents the action as a completed dismissal. The imperfect ἀπεσειόμην describes the ongoing shaking-off action, which Peter addresses with ἀποσειόμενος in the next section.",
          "suggested_revision": "Use “Knowing nothing of the whole situation, I was shaking her off as though she were mad” or the contextually conative “I was trying to shake her off.” Re-review the selected revision in continuity with 12.23.",
