        {
          "source_quote": "οὐ γὰρ δὴ ἐμπορίας ἕνεκα ἢ στρατείας πατρίδας καταλιμπάνειν οἴδατε καὶ εἰς μακροὺς ἀπέρχεσθαι τόπους, διὰ δὲ αἰώνιον σωτηρίαν μηδὲ τριῶν ἡμερῶν ὁδὸν πορευθῆναι θέλειν.",
          "english_quote": "For surely, while you know how to leave your homelands for commerce or military service and go away to distant places, for eternal salvation you are unwilling to travel even a three-days’ journey.",
          "issue": "The initial οὐ has no defensible equivalent in the main wording. Even on an incredulous or rhetorical reading, it rejects or challenges the contrasted behavior; the draft instead affirmatively asserts that the hearers are unwilling to make the journey. The note identifying a rhetorical contrast does not preserve that negative force.",
